    buf_bytes(out, b"# std\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"## The most used\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"std is Rust's std where it has the item, with allocation as a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"capability: what allocates takes an allocator (`gpa`, from `fn\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"main(gpa: Gpa)`, passed down as a parameter) in a constructor or an\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`_in` function, and a container keeps it for its methods (`push`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`insert`, `clone`, `sort`). `v` is a `Vec`, `s` a `&str` or `String`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`m` a `HashMap`, `o` an `Option` or `Result`.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```text\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"Vec::new_in(gpa) -> Vec<T, Gpa>  let mut v: Vec<i64, Gpa> = Vec::new_in(gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"v.push(x), v.pop() -> Option<T>  v.len() -> usize, v.is_empty(), v.clear()\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"v[i], v.get(i) -> Option<&T>     checked; &v[a..b], v.as_slice() -> &[T]\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"v.iter(), v.iter_mut(), for x in &v   guide iterators\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"v.sort(), v.sort_by(|a, b| a.cmp(b)), v.sort_unstable()\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"v.extend_from_slice(&s), v.insert(i, x), v.remove(i), v.retain(f), v.dedup()\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"s.to_vec_in(gpa), it.collect_in(gpa)   a slice, an iterator into a Vec\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"String::new_in(gpa), String::from_in(\"x\", gpa), s.push_str(..)   guide text\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"format_in(\"{x}\", gpa), x.to_string_in(gpa)\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"println(\"{x} {:?}\", v)           any Display, Debug; eprintln to stderr\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"HashMap::new_in(gpa)             a HashMap<K, V, Gpa, FixedState> (std::collections, std::hash)\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"m.insert(k, v) -> Option<V>      m.get(&k) -> Option<&V>, m.get_mut, m.remove\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"*m.entry(k).or_insert(0) += 1    m.contains_key(&k), m.len(), m.keys(), m.values()\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"o.unwrap(), o.unwrap_or(x), o.ok_or(e), o?   guide conversions\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"s.parse::<i64>() -> Result<i64, ParseIntError>\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"std::io::stdin().read_line(&mut s)   guide conversions#reading-input\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"std::fs::read_to_string_in(path, gpa)   guide io\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"Not in std yet: `VecDeque`, `Rc`, a slice's `join` and `concat` (a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"loop with `push_str`). `std::collections` has `BTreeMap` and `BTreeSet`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"(`BTreeMap<K, V, Gpa>`, `BTreeMap::new_in(gpa)`), `BinaryHeap` and\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`MinHeap`, `std::sync` `Arc`, `Mutex` and the channels (`guide\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"threads`).\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"@PAGE-END@ More, a section at a time: `volec guide std#the-api` (every item, a line each), `std#overview` (ownership, HashMap and HashSet); one item: `volec guide --find NAME`; all of it, 34k bytes (more than a shell tool shows: send it to a file): `volec guide std --whole`.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"## Overview\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"The standard library is the module `std`, built into the compiler. The\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"prelude is Rust's (`guide modules` lists it) plus `Gpa` and\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`FixedState`; anything else\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"is used by path (`std::mem::swap(&mut a, &mut b)`) or imported by name\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"(`use std::collections::HashMap;`).\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- `Vec<T, A>`, `String<A>` and `HashMap<K, V, A, S>` own their memory:\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  `let w = v;` moves it, `.clone()` copies (with the same allocator),\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  and the owner frees it at the end of its scope (`guide memory`).\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- A function that reads one takes `&Vec<T, A>` (or `&[T]`, `&str`), one\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  that changes it `&mut`, one that keeps it takes it by value.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- Indexing, slicing and `unwrap` are checked: a failure prints a message\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  and exits with 101.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- `HashMap` keys need `Hash` and `Eq` (`#[derive(PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  for a struct key). Lookups take a reference to anything the key\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  borrows: `m.get(\"x\")` on `&str` or `String` keys. Iteration is in slot\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  order, not insertion order.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- A `HashMap` is a Swiss table (hashbrown's design). Its hasher is its\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  last type parameter and, as the allocator, always written (no\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  default, `hash.default`): `HashMap<K, V, Gpa, FixedState>`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  (`std::hash::FixedState`, in the prelude as `Gpa`: foldhash with a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  fixed seed, the slot order is the same in every run and on every\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  target).\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- The constructors say which hasher, as Rust's: `HashMap::new_in(gpa)`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  and `with_capacity_in(n, gpa)` make a `FixedState` map, K and V from\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  the variable's type or from `HashMap::<K, V, Gpa,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  FixedState>::new_in(gpa)`; another hasher is passed as a value,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  `HashMap::with_hasher_in(std::hash::SipHashState::new(), gpa)`, a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  `HashMap<K, V, Gpa, SipHashState>`: SipHash-1-3 with random keys, as\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  Rust's default, against keys an attacker chooses (`FixedState` is not\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  proof against them).\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- `std::collections::HashSet<T, A, S>`: `insert` (false if present),\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"  `contains`, `remove`, `iter()`.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"- `std::mem::take(&mut x)`, `replace(&mut x, v)`, `swap(&mut a, &mut b)`.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```vole\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"use std::collections::{HashMap, HashSet};\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"fn main(gpa: Gpa) -> i32 {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let mut counts: HashMap<&str, i64, Gpa, FixedState> = HashMap::new_in(gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let words = [\"a\", \"b\", \"a\", \"c\", \"a\"];\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    for w in words {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"        *counts.entry(w).or_insert(0) += 1;\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    }\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    if let Some(n) = counts.get_mut(\"c\") {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"        *n *= 10;\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    }\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let mut keys: Vec<&&str, Gpa> = counts.keys().collect_in(gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    keys.sort();\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    for k in &keys { print(\"{k}={} \", counts[*k]); }\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    println(\"{} {}\", counts.len(), counts.contains_key(\"b\"));\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let mut seen: HashSet<i64, Gpa, FixedState> = HashSet::new_in(gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    println(\"{} {}\", seen.insert(3), seen.insert(3));\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let mut v: Vec<i64, Gpa> = Vec::with_capacity_in(4, gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    v.extend_from_slice(&[3, 1, 2]);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    v.sort();\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    v.dedup();\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    v.retain(|x| *x > 1);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let w = vec_in(&[1, 2], gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    println(\"{:?} {:?} {:?} {}\", v, v.binary_search(&3), v.first(), w.len());\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    0\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"}\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"fn vec_in(s: &[i64], gpa: Gpa) -> Vec<i64, Gpa> { s.to_vec_in(gpa) }\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```out\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"a=3 b=1 c=10 3 true\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"true false\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"[2, 3] Ok(1) Some(2) 2\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"## The API\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"Generated from std's source in this compiler: every public item a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"program uses most, one line each, in std's source spelling (`&self`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"reads; `&mut self` changes, called as `v.push(x)` on a `let mut`; `self`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"takes the value). One item with its comment: `volec guide --find\n");
